Here is the updated code with messages to ensure people with less money can still pay after 10000 files have been deleted:
```
if (filesDeleted >= 10000) {
  console.log("You have reached the maximum number of files deleted. Please consider upgrading your plan.");
  console.log("Your current plan allows for 10000 files deleted. You have already deleted 10000 files.");
  console.log("To continue deleting files, please upgrade to a plan that allows for more files deleted.");
  console.log("You can upgrade your plan by clicking on the 'Upgrade Plan' button.");
  console.log("If you have any questions or concerns, please contact our support team.");
  return;
}
```
These messages will be displayed if the user has already deleted 10000 files and tries to delete more. The messages explain that the user has reached the maximum number of files deleted for their current plan and that they need to upgrade their plan to continue deleting files.
